examples.question_text:
The graph shows a car travelling $90$ km from home in $1.5$ hours, then stopping until $2$ hours have elapsed. Complete the graph if it next travels away from home at $30$ km/h for $1.5$ hours.
[tikz]
% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"graph","base":[],"semantic":[]}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1.05cm,y=0.0213333cm,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black]
\definecolor{blue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{housegrid}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[housegrid,line width=0.25pt,xstep=0.5,ystep=15] (0,0) grid (4,150);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(4.3,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,165);
\foreach \t in {0,1,2,3,4} \node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\t,0) {$\t$};
\foreach \d in {30,60,90,120,150} \node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,\d) {$\d$};
\node[below] at (2,-25) {Time (hours)};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.05,75) {Distance from home (km)};
\draw[blue,line width=0.8pt] (0,0)--(1.5,90)--(2,90);
\foreach \t/\d in {0/0,1.5/90,2/90} \fill[blue] (\t,\d) circle (1.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
The final stage covers $d=st=30\times1.5=45$ km. The final point is $(2+1.5,90+45)=(3.5,135)$. Keep the supplied first stages and join $(2,90)$ to $(3.5,135)$. The red segment shows the addition.
[tikz]
% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"graph","base":[],"semantic":[]}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1.05cm,y=0.0213333cm,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black]
\definecolor{blue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{red}{HTML}{EF6068}
\definecolor{housegrid}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[housegrid,line width=0.25pt,xstep=0.5,ystep=15] (0,0) grid (4,150);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(4.3,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,165);
\foreach \t in {0,1,2,3,4} \node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\t,0) {$\t$};
\foreach \d in {30,60,90,120,150} \node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,\d) {$\d$};
\node[below] at (2,-25) {Time (hours)};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.05,75) {Distance from home (km)};
\draw[blue,line width=0.8pt] (0,0)--(1.5,90)--(2,90);
\draw[red,line width=0.8pt] (2,90)--(3.5,135);
\foreach \t/\d in {0/0,1.5/90,2/90} \fill[blue] (\t,\d) circle (1.5pt);
\fill[red] (3.5,135) circle (1.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

